  "description": "Subject: SSL\u202fvServer\u202fvserver1 \u2013 Current Configuration Summary  \n\nThe virtual server **vserver1** is listening on service port **443** with a clear\u2011text fallback on port **80**. Certificate authority verification is **true**, and the cipher\u2011redirect feature is **ENABLED**, directing clients to the URL **/secure/cipher** when an insecure cipher is detected. Client authentication is **DISABLED**, while client certificates are set to **Optional** and the CRL check is also **Optional**. Diffie\u2011Hellman key exchange is **ENABLED** with a count of **5** and the parameters are loaded from **/etc/ssl/dhparams.pem**; however, the DH key\u2011size limit is **DISABLED** and DHE key exchange with PSK is **NO**. DTLS\u202f1.0 is **ENABLED** but DTLS\u202f1.2 is **DISABLED**; the DTLS flag is **false** and the profile in use is **dtls_profile1**.  \n\nEDNS\u2011RT **ERSA** is **DISABLED** (count **0**). HTTP Strict Transport Security is **ENABLED**, applies to sub\u2011domains (**YES**) and has a max\u2011age of **31536000** seconds. Non\u2011FIPS ciphers are **ENABLED**, OCSP checking is **Mandatory**, and OCSP stapling is **ENABLED**; the site is also listed for preload (**YES**). The push\u2011encryption trigger is set to **Always**, redirect\u2011port rewrite is **ENABLED**, and the server will send a close\u2011notify (**YES**). Session reuse is **ENABLED** with a timeout of **300** seconds. Skip\u2011CA\u2011Name verification is **false**, SNI certificate handling is **true**, and SNI itself is **ENABLED**. SSL\u202fv2 and SSL\u202fv3 are both **DISABLED**. The server uses the **default_ssl_profile**, SSL redirect is **ENABLED**, SSLv2 redirect is **DISABLED**, and the SSLv2 fallback URL is **https://example.com/sslv2**. Strict signature digest checking is **ENABLED**. TLS\u202f1.0 is **DISABLED**, while TLS\u202f1.1, TLS\u202f1.2, and TLS\u202f1.3 are all **ENABLED**; TLS\u202f1.3 session tickets per authentication context are limited to **2**. Finally, zero\u2011RTT early data is **DISABLED**.",
